.TH TEST\-BUP 1 "2026-03-27" "bup" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
test\-bup \- comprehensive test suite for the bup backup utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B test\-bup
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B test\-bup
runs a comprehensive suite of automated tests covering every feature
and command-line flag of
.BR bup (1).
Each test executes in an isolated temporary directory that is
automatically cleaned up on exit.
.PP
Tests that require optional tools
.RB ( gpg ", " bzip2 ", " xz ", " zstd )
are automatically skipped when the tool is not installed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-t " PATTERN" "\fR,\fP \-\-test " PATTERN
Run only tests whose name contains
.IR PATTERN .
The match is case-insensitive and uses substring matching.
Can be specified multiple times; a test runs if it matches
.B any
pattern.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list
List all available test names and exit.
Useful for discovering test names to pass to
.BR \-t .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Show stdout/stderr from each
.B bup
invocation, even for passing tests.
Failing tests always show their output regardless of this flag.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-fail\-fast
Stop on the first test failure instead of continuing to run remaining
tests.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show built-in help and exit.
.SH TEST GROUPS
Tests are organized into the following sections:
.TP
.B BASIC
Core single-directory backup, help flags, and error handling for
missing arguments.
.TP
.B OUTPUT_DIR
The
.B \-o
flag for specifying an alternate output directory.
.TP
.B VERBOSE
The
.B \-v
/
.B \-\-verbose
flag.
.TP
.B EXCLUDE
The
.BR \-x ", " \-\-exclude\-vcs ", " \-\-exclude\-artifacts ", "
.BR \-\-exclude\-secrets ", " \-\-exclude\-dev ", " \-\-show\-excludes ", "
.BR \-\-show\-excluded ", and anchored artifact patterns."
.TP
.B DRY_RUN
The
.B \-n
/
.B \-\-dry\-run
flag and its interaction with other features.
.TP
.B MULTI_DIR
Backing up multiple directories in a single invocation.
.TP
.B COMBINED
The
.B \-\-combined
flag for bundling directories into a single tarball.
.TP
.B COMPRESSION
The
.B \-z
/
.B \-\-compress
flag with gzip, bzip2, xz, and zstd.
.TP
.B ENCRYPTION
The
.B \-e
/
.B \-\-encrypt
and
.B \-\-recipient
flags (requires gpg).
.TP
.B RETENTION
The
.B \-\-keep
and
.B \-\-prune
flags for backup retention management.
.TP
.B LIST
The
.B \-\-list
and
.B \-L
/
.B \-\-list\-verbose
flags.
.TP
.B SAVE_SCRIPT
The
.BR \-s ", " \-S ", and " \-d
flags for generating re-runnable backup scripts.
.TP
.B PRE_POST
Automatic execution of
.B .bup\-pre.sh
and
.B .bup\-post.sh
scripts.
.TP
.B NAMING
Automatic conflict-free naming with numeric suffixes, and self-exclusion
when the tarball is created inside the target directory.
.TP
.B ATOMIC
Atomic write behavior (temporary file + mv).
Verifies no temp files remain after a successful backup.
.TP
.B SIZE_REPORT
Verification that backup size is reported after creation.
.TP
.B COLOR
Color output support, including
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable and pipe detection.
.TP
.B BACKWARD_COMPAT
Backward compatibility with the original invocation style.
.TP
.B ERROR
Error handling for invalid inputs (unknown options, missing arguments).
.SH TEST ASSETS
.B test\-bup
uses static fixture directories in the
.B test\-assets/
directory alongside the script:
.TP
.B project\-simple
A minimal project with source files and documentation.
.TP
.B project\-artifacts
A project containing common build artifacts (node_modules, target,
\&.cache), secrets (.env, appsettings.json), and VCS files (.git).
.TP
.B project\-scripts
A project with working .bup\-pre.sh and .bup\-post.sh scripts.
.TP
.B project\-fail\-pre
A project whose .bup\-pre.sh always exits with failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colored test output.
Also set implicitly for each
.B bup
invocation during testing to ensure deterministic output matching.
.TP
.B BUP_PATH
Override the path to the
.B bup
binary under test.
Defaults to
.B ./bup
relative to the test\-bup script.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All tests passed or were skipped.
.TP
.B 1
One or more tests failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
test\-bup                          # run all tests
test\-bup \-t compress              # run only compression tests
test\-bup \-t exclude \-t retain     # run exclude and retention tests
test\-bup \-l                       # list all test names
test\-bup \-v                       # show output from all tests
test\-bup \-v \-x                    # verbose, stop on first failure
test\-bup \-t basic \-v              # run basic tests with verbose output
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bup (1)
